From d4167e5b11ea20ecf6205bfaaae873eacf9481ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 15:31:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add deep links that import shared schedules from jupiterp.com
 links

The Jupiterp web planner (atcupps/Jupiterp#933) shares schedules as
https://jupiterp.com/?s=2~<packed segments>. Opening one of those links
on a device with this app now opens the app and imports the schedule:

- Port the web ShareLink codec to commonMain (schema v1 literal and v2
  base62-packed [number:10|suffix:5|section:14] segments), including
  cross-implementation test vectors computed with the web ShareLink.ts
  so the two clients can never drift apart silently.
- On open, decode the token, re-fetch the courses from the API, save
  the result as a new "Shared schedule" (numbered when taken), and open
  the saved-schedules sheet so the user can switch to it. The user's
  current schedule is never replaced; stale sections are skipped with a
  notice, and network failures surface a retry hint.
- Android: autoVerify App Links intent filter for jupiterp.com and
  www.jupiterp.com plus a jupiterp:// fallback scheme; singleTask
  MainActivity routes cold-start and onNewIntent URLs into common code.
- iOS: Universal Links via an Associated Domains entitlement plus a
  jupiterp:// URL scheme, both funneled through onOpenURL /
  onContinueUserActivity into the shared DeepLinkHandler.
- ScheduleRepository: add awaitInitialLoad() so a deep link import at
  cold start cannot clobber schedules still loading from storage.
- docs/DEEP_LINKS.md documents the assetlinks.json / AASA files that
  jupiterp.com must serve for OS-level link verification, and how to
  test before they are deployed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
